## MSBuild Testing Best Practices
1. Always use the `MSBuildCollectionFixture` for tests that require `MSBuildWorkspace`:
   ```csharp
   [Collection(MSBuildCollectionFixture.Name)]
   public class YourTestClass : IDisposable
   {
       private readonly MSBuildWorkspace _workspace;
       
       public YourTestClass(ITestOutputHelper outputHelper, MSBuildFixture fixture)
       {
           _workspace = fixture.Workspace;
       }
   }
   ```

2. Benefits of using the collection fixture:
   - Ensures MSBuild initialization happens exactly once
   - Prevents parallel execution of MSBuild-dependent tests
   - Properly manages workspace lifecycle
   - Avoids "MSBuild already loaded" errors

3. Common patterns:
   ```csharp
   // For solution analysis tests
   var solution = await _workspace.OpenSolutionAsync(solutionPath);
   
   // For project analysis tests
   var project = await _workspace.OpenProjectAsync(projectPath);
   ```

4. Example test structure:
   ```csharp
   [Collection(MSBuildCollectionFixture.Name)]
   public class DependencyTests : IDisposable
   {
       private readonly MSBuildWorkspace _workspace;
       private readonly DisposableRepository _repository;

       public DependencyTests(MSBuildFixture fixture)
       {
           _workspace = fixture.Workspace;
           _repository = new DisposableRepository();
       }

       public void Dispose()
       {
           _repository?.Dispose();
       }

       [Fact]
       public async Task AnalyzeDependencies_ShouldWork()
       {
           // Test implementation
       }
   }
   ```

